 "final": true,
 "findings": [
  {
   "file": "modules/finance/server/time-sync.ts",
   "fp": "53ddd8fbad9c",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 21,
   "message": "Change 073 lets people log hours on Saturday and Sunday (`log_time` with `weekend: true`, and change-request additions). `monthsOfWeek` still recalculates only the months of Monday and Friday (`[0, 4]`). When a week's weekend falls in the next month, approved billable Sunday hours are never added to that month's T&M billable figure or its draft. Fix: build the month set from all seven days (`[0..6]`), or from the distinct months of the week's live entries. Add a test where the approved weekend hours fall in the next month.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "Week 2026-W44 runs Mon Oct 26 to Sun Nov 1. Kasun logs 4 billable hours on Fleet Tracker on Sun 2026-11-01 (weekend: true), and the week is approved. `time.week.approved` recalculates only 2026-10, so November's `finance.billable` for Fleet Tracker misses the 4 hours and its invoice draft is short by 4 \u00d7 rate. Reopen and locked-change events miss them the same way.",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "file": "modules/career/module.ts",
   "fp": "7b15e659f73b",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 33,
   "message": "Several new `keep` exemptions take columns that hold personal data out of retention and erasure, and their own reason text says so: `career.history.detail` (\"Anonymising its personal keys is a 070 follow-up\"), `delivery.proposal.meta` (\"Personal keys are a 070 follow-up\") and `it_access.change.detail` (\"Its directory user id is a 070 follow-up\"). This is the same pattern as the earlier blocker lesson, where personal data was moved into `keep`. Erasure and the 7-year anonymisation never reach these values, which breaks the 032 module standard. Fix: anonymise the personal keys inside these JSON columns (a key-level rule) in this change. Until then, list the columns in `fields`. Do not use `keep` for data you know is personal.",
   "original_severity": "blocker",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "An erasure request for the person named in a career event's `detail` (or the directory user id in `it_access.change.detail`) completes. `career.history.detail` still holds their personal keys, and so do the other two columns.",
   "severity": "blocker"
  },
  {
   "file": "modules/time/server/decide-card.ts",
   "fp": "10847c367160",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 23,
   "message": "This card check writes the 24-hours-a-day limit a second time, as a float comparison: `Number(total) + hours > 24`. The service enforces the same rule through `guardDayTotal`, which counts in hundredths so that 23.95 + 0.05 is exactly 24. Floating-point error can make the two disagree: the card refuses an addition that the service, and `request-add`'s own check, would accept. Fix: call `guardDayTotal` (or one shared function) from the card check instead of copying the rule.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "A person has entries on a day that add up to just under 24 hours and asks to add the remainder, and the float sum of the two comes out a hair above 24. `request_time_addition` passes, because `guardDayTotal` counts in hundredths. The approver's apply card is then refused with \"more than 24 h\", so the request can never be applied.",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "file": "apps/web/app/actions/chat.ts",
   "fp": "19238fd61dce",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 39,
   "message": "`pageContext` returns `null` both for a page with no module route and for a failed read: a database error, or `SignedInElsewhere`. `forPins` and `usable` likewise turn errors into \"no suggestions\". The chat header and suggestions then show the generic \"nothing here\" state when the read actually failed. Return a distinct failed state, or at least surface `SignedInElsewhere`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "`pageInfo` throws because the database is unavailable. The chat header shows \"Ask, add or drop anything here\" with no suggestions, which looks exactly like a page that has none.",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "modules/time/README.md",
   "fp": "895a722f6a82",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 11,
   "message": "The README contradicts itself and the code. The Logging bullet still says a day \"must be Monday to Friday\", but the 073 bullets allow weekends with `weekend: true`. The \"Allocated hours \u2026 are 40 h per person until allocations (010) publishes capacity\" line is also out of date: `capacityOf` now uses allocations \u00d7 each person's weekly target. Update both lines.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B10",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "apps/web/components/chat/Chat.tsx",
   "fp": "3b5a9012d010",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 74,
   "message": "The fresh-open effect records the new `fresh` value before it checks `busy`, and then returns. A fresh open while a turn is still running is therefore lost for good: the old conversation, pins and prompt stay. Check `busy` first, and record the value only once the reset has actually run. Separately, now that a pin replaces all pins (`setPins([pin])`), the earlier `ask.added` and pin-filter logic is dead code.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "The person presses Ctrl+K to start a new chat while amax is still replying. When the reply arrives, chat still shows the previous conversation and pins instead of a fresh one.",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "modules/time/server/request.ts",
   "fp": "c0fc7f31343e",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 22,
   "message": "A request to add hours (073, `kind: 'add'`) is routed and scoped by `weekProjectIds`, which lists only projects that already have hours in the week. The same applies to `reviews()`/`chainFor` in `requests-read.ts`. But applying the request needs `mayAddOn`, meaning the reviewer approves the project being added. When that project has no hours in the week yet, its PM is neither notified nor allowed to see or decide the request. Any reviewer who can see it may then be refused at apply. Fix: add the requested project (`proposed.projectId`) to the notification's `projectIds` and to the reviewer check for add requests.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "design",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "Kasun's submitted week has only Contoso Portal hours. He calls `request_time_addition` for 2 h on Fleet Tracker. Nimal, PM of Fleet Tracker and not Kasun's manager, gets no bell and `get_change_requests` does not show him the request. A reviewer through Contoso Portal who doesn't approve Fleet Tracker sees the request but is refused at apply. Only an unscoped Admin can apply it.",
   "severity": "major"
  }
 ],
